# Confidently Incorrect

Binding rules are in `.ai/rules.md`. Read that file before any
non-trivial change. If a request contradicts a recorded decision in
`architecture.md`, stop and say so.

Never:

- Hardcode a league-derived value (`.ai/rules.md` §4)
- Let model output reach the Yahoo API unvalidated
- Add a deterministic quality floor to trade acceptance
- Skip the `considered_options` snapshot
- Let real names enter `kb.db`, `notes/`, logs, prompts, or MQTT
- Include `notes/managers/` in a site build
- Commit secrets
- Swallow an exception on a write path
- Ping the dead-man switch on process start
- Touch `/srv/ci/` with a git command
- Deploy by improvising SSH instead of `deploy.sh`

Docs are the spec. Append to the decision log; never edit an old
entry to match new behaviour. New unknowns go in `followups.md`.
